The doctor writes the prescription.
I sit calmly for a moment.
I ask him, "Doctor, is it anything serious?"
He smiles and says, "No madam, do not worry."
"This is just a viral infection caused by the changing season."
"Because of the first rains, many people are falling ill nowadays."
He writes the names of some medicines on a paper.
He gives me some advice about the illness.
"You should drink plenty of warm water all day," he says.
"You should not eat anything from outside right now."
"For the next few days, you should eat only light food."
"And you should rest as much as possible."
I listen to his words carefully.
He gives me the medicine prescription.
"Take these medicines for three days, you will feel better soon."
The doctor's words reassure me.
I thank him.
I thank the doctor and come out of the clinic.
